  "body": "Fixes #337886\n\n## What\n\n`buildOptions` passed `disallowedTools: ['WebSearch']` for every Claude session. The reason, per `roadmap.md`, is that CAPI doesn't support WebSearch, which only applies when the SDK is routed through the Copilot proxy. Native (Anthropic-auth) sessions talk to Anthropic directly, where WebSearch works, so they were losing web search for no reason.\n\nThe block now applies only when `transport.kind === 'proxy'`, using the `isProxy` flag `buildOptions` already computes for the other transport-specific options. The two roadmap lines describing the setting are updated to match.\n\n## How to test\n\n- Unit tests added in `claudeSdkOptions.test.ts`: the proxy transport still sets `disallowedTools: ['WebSearch']`; the native transport leaves it unset.\n- Manually: in a Claude session authenticated with `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN` or `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, ask for a web search. Before the change the model has no WebSearch tool; after it, the search runs and returns results. Copilot-routed sessions are unchanged.\n\nI tested the native behaviour by applying the same change to the built 1.139.0 `agentHostMain.js`; I haven't run the unit tests locally.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_015wqjvswfjKqx3aDMsuMiBG\n",
  "rebaseable": true
 },
